    evidence: "In: the list of types the plays need, each with its one-line meaning: Business Intent, Epic, Story, Bug, Chore, Spike." and "Out: a record of what was made and what was mapped." The six one-line meanings the brief must show are never given, and the record has no named place. Rules & behavior covers yes, no, all-present and cannot-make, but not these branches: the product owner approves only some of the missing types; making a type fails (for example the account lacks the rights to add an organization-level type on GitHub); initialize runs again when a mapping already exists.
    fix:      In Inputs / Outputs, write the one-line meaning of each of the six types (for example "Spike: a time-boxed look into an unknown, with a finding as its result") and name where the record is kept (for example beside the mapping in the project's settings). In Rules & behavior, add one line each for: a partial yes (make only the approved types; the rest stay missing and are named in the brief); a make that fails (say what failed in plain words, make nothing further for that type, leave it unmapped so plays stop with the initialize message); and a run where a mapping already exists (keep it, show it in the brief, and change it only on a new yes), pointing to fn-rerun-initialize for the rest of the re-run.
